  "question": {
    "text": "If the sum of first $n$ terms of an $\\mathrm{AP}$ is $\\mathrm{cn}^2$, then the sum of squares of these $n$ terms is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "d8mgh",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{n\\left(4 n^2-1\\right) c^2}{6}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9FLGY",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{n\\left(4 n^2+1\\right) c^2}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "I4wzM",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{n\\left(4 n^2-1\\right) c^2}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "O6CAT",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{n\\left(4 n^2+1\\right) c^2}{6}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $S_n=c^2$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& S_{n-1}=c(n-1)^2=c n^2+c-2 c n \\\\\n& \\therefore T_n=2 c n-c \\quad\\left(\\because T_n=S_n-S_{n-1}\\right) \\\\\n& T_n^2=(2 c n-c)^2=4 c^2 n^2+c^2-4 c^2 n \\\\\n& \\therefore \\text { Sum }=\\Sigma T_n^2=\\frac{4 c^2 \\cdot n(n+1)(2 n+1)}{6} \\\\\n& =\\frac{2 c^2 n(n+1)(2 n+1)+3 n c^2-6 c^2 n(n+1)}{3} \\\\\n& =\\frac{n c^2\\left[4 n^2+6 n+2+3-6 n-6\\right]}{3} \\\\\n& =\\frac{n c^2\\left(4 n^2-1\\right)}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
